# ============================================================
# Merge behaviour. This file exists because two people work on this
# repo at once, and most of what looked like "git being difficult"
# was really git being asked to merge things it cannot merge.
# ============================================================

# ---- Line endings ----
#
# `text=auto` on its own normalises to LF *in the repository* but lets
# each checkout use whatever its platform prefers. Two machines with
# different preferences then produce diffs where every line has
# changed, and a one-line edit becomes a whole-file conflict. `eol=lf`
# pins the working tree as well, so both sides always see the same
# bytes.
#
# Every tracked text file here is already LF, so this normalises
# nothing today and changes no content. It stops the problem starting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- Binaries ----
#
# Git must never attempt a line-wise merge on these, and a textual
# diff of a WOFF2 is noise. Marked binary so a clash is reported
# honestly as "both changed, pick one" instead of a corrupted file.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary

# ---- Generated files ----
#
# Never hand-resolve a conflict in either of these. Take one side and
# regenerate:
#
#   package-lock.json                  git checkout --theirs -- package-lock.json && npm install
#   python/.../data/manifest.json      npm run spec:sync
#
# The manifest copy inside the package is written by scripts/sync-spec.js
# from spec/manifest.json, which is the only one to edit by hand. CI
# fails if the two have drifted, so regenerating is always correct.
package-lock.json                          -diff linguist-generated
python/thehallucinatedlab/data/manifest.json -diff linguist-generated

# ---- Vendored ----
#
# GSAP is checked in deliberately (self-hosted, was cdnjs). It is not
# our code; keep it out of diffs and out of the language stats.
assets/vendor/** -diff linguist-vendored
